{
  "_comment": [
    "Differential pin for the TWO canonicalizer implementations (issue #1455).",
    "",
    "canonical.py and canonical.mjs are independent implementations of one",
    "written spec. Two implementations are only KNOWN to agree if something",
    "checks; this table is that check. Every vector is materialized into each",
    "leg's NATIVE value shape and canonicalized by that leg's adapter; all",
    "three must produce `canonical` exactly.",
    "",
    "Leg value encoding: plain JSON where the native type is already JSON",
    "(bool/number/string/null); otherwise a tagged object materialized by",
    "vectors.py / vectors.mjs:",
    "  {\"$\":\"uuid\"|\"decimal\"|\"inet\"|\"bigint\"|\"date\", \"v\": ...}",
    "  {\"$\":\"bytes\", \"hex\": ...}   {\"$\":\"datetime\", \"ms\": ...}",
    "  {\"$\":\"duration\", \"months\":..., \"days\":..., \"nanos\": \"...\"}",
    "  {\"$\":\"list\"|\"set\"|\"tuple\", \"items\": [...]}",
    "  {\"$\":\"map\", \"entries\": [[k, v], ...]}",
    "The `cli` leg needs no tags -- its values are already parsed JSON.",
    "",
    "A `cli` value of null means 'this shape is unreachable from the CLI'; the",
    "vector then pins only the python and node legs. That is used ONLY for a",
    "value the CLI cannot emit, never to excuse a divergence.",
    "",
    "`rows` (issue #1455, F1) drives the ROW path rather than a single value:",
    "each case declares `columns` (name -> CQL type) plus a per-leg ROW object,",
    "and every leg must canonicalize to the same `canonical` ROW. It exists",
    "because a column NAME can be hostile -- `__proto__` is a legal quoted CQL",
    "identifier -- and the value vectors never touch a column-name-keyed object.",
    "Expressible as data precisely because JSON.parse and json.loads create an",
    "OWN `__proto__` property where a JS object literal would not.",
    "",
    "Two node-only spec tags exist for REFUSAL cases (issue #1455, F5/F6):",
    "  {\"$\":\"undefined\"}    -- a PRESENT property holding `undefined`.",
    "  {\"$\":\"duration_raw\"} -- a duration object whose months/days/nanos are",
    "                          materialized INDIVIDUALLY (a bare JSON number",
    "                          becomes a JS number, a {\"$\":\"bigint\"} tag a",
    "                          BigInt), so a case can plant the wrong JS type on",
    "                          one field. The plain {\"$\":\"duration\"} tag always",
    "                          produces the CORRECT shape and is what value",
    "                          vectors use."
  ],
  "floor": {
    "_comment": [
      "B2 / #3544's own lesson: an empty or truncated subject set must never",
      "report green. Both vectors.py and vectors.mjs enforce this floor before",
      "reporting, so `0/0 vectors OK` is unreachable.",
      "`required_kinds` is checked against the CQL type KINDS appearing anywhere",
      "in a vector's parsed type tree, so deleting every blob vector reds the",
      "runners rather than shrinking the suite silently.",
      "`rows` pins the ROW-BUILDING path (types_from_columns/typesFromColumns +",
      "canon_row_*), which the value vectors cannot reach; min_rows and",
      "required_row_names keep it from being emptied.",
      "`required_error_names` names the STRICTNESS refusals (F4 containers, F5 the",
      "node integer surface, F6 a present `undefined`) rather than counting them:",
      "each pins a defect that is silent when it is not refused, so a count alone",
      "would let one be swapped for a benign case."
    ],
    "min_vectors": 74,
    "min_errors": 46,
